![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When generating artifact receipts, check if the file exists before attempting to calculate its hash (e.g., SHA-256) to prevent raw file system errors (like ENOENT) from crashing the script when optional files are missing. If the file is missing, record the hash as null.

```javascript
function sha256File(root, relPath) {
  const target = resolvePath(root, relPath);
  if (!target || !fs.existsSync(target)) {
    return null;
  }
  try {
    return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(target)).digest('hex');
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When generating artifact receipts, check if the file exists before attempting to calculate its hash (e.g., SHA-256) to prevent raw file system errors (like ENOENT) from crashing the script when optional files are missing. If the file is missing, record the hash as null and preserve the existence metadata.
</details>

