![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Add defensive guards to ensure `inputDiagnostics` is treated as an array, and filter `candidateRows` to only valid objects before mapping over them to prevent potential `TypeErrors`.

```javascript
  const diagnosticsArray = Array.isArray(inputDiagnostics) ? inputDiagnostics : [];
  const criticalDiagnostics = diagnosticsArray.filter((diagnostic) => diagnostic?.severity === 'critical');
  const candidateRows = (Array.isArray(pilot.candidates) ? pilot.candidates : [])
    .filter((row) => row && typeof row === 'object');
  const ids = candidateRows.map((row) => row.candidate_id);
  const sortedIds = [...ids].sort(compareByteOrder);
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When filtering or mapping arrays of objects, use defensive guards (such as checking if the element is a valid object) to ignore nullish or malformed elements instead of throwing a TypeError.
</details>

